<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26034" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διάτᾰσις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>tension, dilatation,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔχειν δ.</span> to have the <i>power of
				dilatation,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>PA</u>
				664a33
			</span></i> (v.l.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεφαλῆς διατάσεις καὶ ἰλίγγους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					407c
				</span></i>
			 (prob.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>extension,</i> of a fractured or dislocated limb, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Off.</u>
				15
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Heliod.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				49.8.33
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπαρτῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alciphr.
					2.4
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>stretching across</i>: hence Medic., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. φρενῶν</span>”
				<i>diaphragm,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>VM</u>
					22
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ.</span> alone, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Coac.</u>
				394
			</span></i>; also of vaginal <i>obstruction,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Paul.Aeg.
				6.72
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>tension, exertion,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πνεύματος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>Sud.</u>
					32
				</span></i>
			; of athletes and the like , <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				885b23
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IA</u>
				705a18
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διατάσεις καὶ κλαυθμοί,</span>
			of infants, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1336a34
			</span></i>: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ εὔνοια . . οὐκ ἔχει δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>EN</u>
					1166b33
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν δ. γενομένης τῆς ψυχῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Cor.</u>
					21
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ πρὸς τὸν ἥλιον δ.,</span> of
			plants, <i><span class="en">
				Iamb.
				<u>Protr.</u>
				21
			</span></i>.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λή.</span>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>contention, quarrel,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς μεγάλην ἐλθεῖν δ. πρός τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					38
				</span></i>
			/<i><span class="en">
				9.2
			</span></i>(s.v.l.).</div>
